Sebasti?n,

When you ran the model in SPSS, was it estimated via REML or ML? Perhaps
you're running into a difference in the default settings for the estimation
method between SPSS and R. That's one of the first things I look for when
different software packages give different answers for what I think is
supposed to be the same model run on the same data. 


